<title>UK: Carlton stacks up 11 pct H1 profit rise.</title>
<headline>Carlton stacks up 11 pct H1 profit rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		17.3		   vs 15.3</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 4.9		    vs 4.37</p>
<p> Pretax		     158.6		  vs 143.3</p>
<p> Turnover		   896.0		  vs 847.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits in a range between 171.8 and 155.0 million stg.</p>
<p>Earnings per share were headline. Before an exceptional loss of an associate relating to the closure of Channel KTV for which there was no tax relief, pre-tax profit rose 13 pct to 163 million stg.</p>
<p>Full company name - Carlton Communications Plc</p>
</text>
